# Netlify response headers — the primary home for this site's security headers.
#
# Everything in `public/` is copied verbatim to the root of `dist/`, and Netlify
# reads `_headers` from the root of the publish directory.
#
# WHY HEADERS AND NOT ONLY THE <meta> TAG IN index.html
#
#   · `frame-ancestors` is ignored when delivered via <meta>. Clickjacking
#     protection is only real as a header, which is the reason this file exists.
#   · A header covers every response, not just the HTML document.
#   · It applies before the document is parsed, rather than partway through
#     <head>.
#
# The <meta> CSP in index.html is kept as a narrower fallback, for when `dist/`
# is served by something that ignores this file — `vite preview`, a plain static
# server, or a different host. The two policies must be kept in step; see the
# comment in index.html.
#
# THE POLICY, LINE BY LINE
#
#   default-src 'self'       nothing loads from any other origin.
#   script-src  'self'       no inline scripts, no eval, no third-party JS.
#                            `build.modulePreload.polyfill` is off in
#                            vite.config.ts so the build emits no inline script.
#   style-src   'self'       CSS Modules compile to an external stylesheet, and
#                            the species plates use SVG presentation attributes
#                            rather than inline styles, so nothing here needs
#                            'unsafe-inline'.
#   img-src     'self' data: covers the small assets Vite inlines as data URIs.
#   font-src    'self'       fonts are self-hosted; no font CDN is contacted.
#   connect-src 'self'       the archive is static. Nothing phones home.
#   object-src  'none'       no plugins, ever.
#   frame-ancestors 'none'   the site cannot be framed. Header-only.
#
#   X-Content-Type-Options   trust the declared Content-Type; stop the browser
#                            deciding for itself that a response is a script.
#   Referrer-Policy          full URL same-origin, bare origin cross-origin,
#                            nothing at all when downgrading HTTPS to HTTP.
#   Permissions-Policy       the archive uses none of these features, so each is
#                            denied outright rather than left at the browser
#                            default. An empty allowlist `()` means no origin at
#                            all, including this one.
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy
#                            puts the document in its own browsing context
#                            group, so a window it opened — or one that opened
#                            it — cannot reach in through `window.opener`.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security is deliberately absent: Netlify issues it
# automatically for sites on HTTPS, and setting it by hand risks pinning a
# max-age that outlives the certificate setup.
#
# Format: an unindented path pattern, then indented `Name: value` lines. Keep
# comments unindented and outside the block — indented `#` lines inside a block
# are not reliably treated as comments.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
